# core.autocrlf=true on a Windows checkout rewrites shell scripts to CRLF, and
# bash in WSL then fails on $'\r': command not found. ops/wsl-start.sh is RUN FROM
# this working tree by the TechTrend scheduled task, so its line endings are
# not cosmetic -- CRLF makes it unrunnable on the only host that runs it.
*.sh text eol=lf
